WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.900
A POT file holds the source strings,

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.928
and each PO file pairs them with
one language's translations.

3
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.795
General Translation writes a
translated PO file for each language

4
00:00:12.795 --> 00:00:14.756
from your POT template.

5
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.772
Fill every msgstr,
including each plural form,

6
00:00:19.772 --> 00:00:23.313
and keep msgid, msgctxt,

7
00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:25.286
and placeholders unchanged.

8
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.772
Add a pot entry to gt.config.json
with the PO transformation

9
00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:30.421
format.

10
00:00:30.821 --> 00:00:35.999
Then npx gt translate fills
every plural form Polish needs,

11
00:00:35.999 --> 00:00:36.776
three in all.

12
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.309
Run msgfmt with the check flag,

13
00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:41.340
and check that no msgstr is empty.

14
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.005
Your team now ships
Polish with each release.
